      <p class="section__text">
        Embroidery complexity affects decoration costs. Simple logos under 5,000 stitches cost minimal amounts, while complex designs exceeding 20,000 stitches require significant machine time and increase pricing. Thread count also impacts cost - standard 5-color embroidery costs less than 12-color designs. Packaging type adds variable costs: basic polybags add minimal cost, while retail-ready boxes with custom tissue paper can increase per-unit costs by 5-10%. Geographic destination affects landed cost through shipping and duty considerations - Bangladesh offers duty-free access to EU markets through 2026, reducing landed costs for European buyers. Understanding these cost drivers helps you optimize specifications for your target price point.
      </p>
